   "source": [
    "# SBN Tool Selection: Semantic Matching vs LangChain ReAct\n",
    "\n",
    "Compares two approaches to tool selection in the SBN InvestigationLoopAgent:\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Approach A | Approach B |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Name** | Semantic Matching (DyTopo) | LangChain ReAct |\n",
    "| **Tool selection** | `cosine(query_vec, tool_key_vec) > τ` | LLM reads docstrings, reasons which tool to call |\n",
    "| **ML inside tool selection** | Yes — sentence embeddings | No — pure LLM reasoning |\n",
    "| **Control flow** | Explicit 5-phase loop | LangChain manages ReAct loop |\n",
    "| **LLM calls per round** | 1 (investigator only) | 1+ (LLM also decides tool) |\n",
    "| **Determinism** | High | Lower — LLM may vary |\n",
    "| **Auditability** | Full cosine scores logged | Depends on callbacks |\n",
    "\n",
    "Both use **identical mock tool responses** — only the selection mechanism differs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 1: Install dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Approach A needs: sentence-transformers, numpy\n",
    "# Approach B needs: langchain, langchain-anthropic (or langchain-openai)\n",
    "%pip install -q sentence-transformers numpy pandas\n",
    "%pip install -q langchain langchain-anthropic langchain-core"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 2: Shared mock tool responses ────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Both approaches call the same mock functions.\n",
    "# In production these would be httpx.get() calls to the Java Invoice Service.\n",
    "\n",
    "PAYLOAD_ID = \"INV-78432\"\n",
    "ORG_ID     = \"BNO-456001\"\n",
    "QUESTION   = \"Why did INV-78432 fail routing?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mock responses keyed by tool name — deterministic for fair comparison\n",
    "_MOCK_RESPONSES = {\n",
    "    \"FlowLogTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Steps: DocReceived OK, SchemaValidation OK, RoutingLookup OK, \"\n",
    "        \"RoutingPublishStep FAILED at 09:14:32. error_code: DESTINATION_NULL.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"KafkaOffsetTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Kafka message produced: YES. Consumer offset: never consumed. \"\n",
    "        \"Partition 3, offset 88441. delivered_downstream: false.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"RoutingDecisionTool\": (\n",
    "        \"routing_method: DIRECT_POST. destination_url: null. \"\n",
    "        \"buyer_org_id: BNO-456001. routing_rule_matched: false.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"OrgConfigTool\": (\n",
    "        \"postURL: '' (empty). routing_enabled: true. \"\n",
    "        \"last_modified: 2026-09-14T11:22:00Z. network_id: null.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Shared mock HTTP functions (replace with httpx.get() in production) ───────\n",
    "def _call_flow_log(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return _MOCK_RESPONSES[\"FlowLogTool\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "def _call_kafka_offset(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return _MOCK_RESPONSES[\"KafkaOffsetTool\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "def _call_routing_decision(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return _MOCK_RESPONSES[\"RoutingDecisionTool\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "def _call_org_config(org_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return _MOCK_RESPONSES[\"OrgConfigTool\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Mock tool responses ready.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Approach A — Semantic Matching (DyTopo style)\n",
    "\n",
    "Tool selection: `cosine(investigator_query_embedding, tool_key_embedding) > τ`\n",
    "\n",
    "The LLM never sees the tool list. It outputs a natural-language query.\n",
    "The embedding model matches that query against pre-computed tool key vectors.\n",
    "Tools with cosine score above threshold τ are activated — no LLM call for routing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 3A: Tool key descriptors + pre-compute embeddings ────────────────────\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
    "\n",
    "# Static key descriptors — what each tool PROVIDES\n",
    "# Written once; never changes at runtime\n",
    "TOOL_KEYS = {\n",
    "    \"FlowLogTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Provides the full step-by-step routing flow trace for a document, \"\n",
    "        \"showing which routing steps executed, which step failed, and at what timestamp.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"KafkaOffsetTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Reports whether a document message was produced to Kafka, the current \"\n",
    "        \"consumer offset, and whether the message was ever delivered downstream.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"RoutingDecisionTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Returns the routing decision record: the routing method used, the destination \"\n",
    "        \"PostURL, the buyer orgId, and whether a valid routing rule was matched.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"OrgConfigTool\": (\n",
    "        \"Returns the buyer organisation's current OrgPreferences: the active PostURL, \"\n",
    "        \"routing flags, feature toggles, and the last-modified timestamp.\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pre-compute tool key embeddings once (pod startup in production)\n",
    "_encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\n",
    "\n",
    "TOOL_KEY_EMBEDDINGS = {}\n",
    "for name, text in TOOL_KEYS.items():\n",
    "    vec = _encoder.encode([text], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]\n",
    "    TOOL_KEY_EMBEDDINGS[name] = np.array(vec, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Tool key embeddings pre-computed:\")\n",
    "for name, vec in TOOL_KEY_EMBEDDINGS.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {name}: shape={vec.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 4A: Semantic match function ──────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "TAU = 0.35   # cosine threshold — tune this in ablation\n",
    "\n",
    "def match_tools_semantic(investigator_query: str, tau: float = TAU):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Embed the investigator query, score against each tool key embedding.\n",
    "    Return (activated_tools, scores_dict).\n",
    "    No LLM call — pure vector arithmetic.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    q_vec = _encoder.encode([investigator_query], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]\n",
    "    q_vec = np.array(q_vec, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "    scores = {\n",
    "        name: float(np.dot(q_vec, key_emb))\n",
    "        for name, key_emb in TOOL_KEY_EMBEDDINGS.items()\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    activated = [name for name, score in scores.items() if score > tau]\n",
    "    return activated, scores\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Demo: 3 investigator queries (same as the mock worked example) ────────────\n",
    "queries = [\n",
    "    \"What routing steps executed for INV-78432 and where did the process stop?\",\n",
    "    \"What routing method and destination PostURL was configured for buyer BNO-456001?\",\n",
    "    \"Is the buyer BNO-456001 PostURL currently blank and has it been blank since September?\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'Query (truncated)':<55} {'Activated tools':<45} {'Scores'}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 130)\n",
    "for q in queries:\n",
    "    activated, scores = match_tools_semantic(q)\n",
    "    score_str = \"  \".join(f\"{n}={s:.2f}\" for n, s in scores.items())\n",
    "    print(f\"{q[:54]:<55} {str(activated):<45} {score_str}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 5A: Full Approach A investigation loop ───────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Replaces the LLM investigator with scripted queries (mock mode).\n",
    "# Tool selection is always the real cosine matching — this is what we are evaluating.\n",
    "\n",
    "import time\n",
    "from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n",
    "\n",
    "@dataclass\n",
    "class RoundResultA:\n",
    "    round: int\n",
    "    query: str\n",
    "    activated_tools: list\n",
    "    tool_scores: dict\n",
    "    tool_results: dict\n",
    "    confidence: float\n",
    "    halt: bool\n",
    "    halt_reason: str\n",
    "    llm_calls: int      # investigator calls only (tool selection uses no LLM)\n",
    "    latency_ms: float\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scripted investigator queries (mock — in production these come from LLM)\n",
    "_MOCK_QUERIES = [\n",
    "    (\"What routing steps executed for INV-78432 and where did the process stop?\",   0.10),\n",
    "    (\"What routing method and destination PostURL was configured for BNO-456001?\",  0.45),\n",
    "    (\"Is the buyer BNO-456001 PostURL currently blank since September?\",             0.95),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "TOOL_DISPATCH = {\n",
    "    \"FlowLogTool\":       lambda: _call_flow_log(PAYLOAD_ID),\n",
    "    \"KafkaOffsetTool\":   lambda: _call_kafka_offset(PAYLOAD_ID),\n",
    "    \"RoutingDecisionTool\": lambda: _call_routing_decision(PAYLOAD_ID),\n",
    "    \"OrgConfigTool\":     lambda: _call_org_config(ORG_ID),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 0.90\n",
    "T_MAX = 5\n",
    "\n",
    "results_A = []\n",
    "total_llm_calls_A = 0\n",
    "total_tool_calls_A = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Approach A: Semantic Matching ===\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "for round_t, (query, confidence) in enumerate(_MOCK_QUERIES):\n",
    "    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Phase 1 — investigator (mock; costs 1 LLM call in production)\n",
    "    total_llm_calls_A += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Phase 2 — semantic match (no LLM; cosine only)\n",
    "    activated, scores = match_tools_semantic(query, tau=TAU)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Phase 3 — tool dispatch (mock HTTP)\n",
    "    tool_results = {name: TOOL_DISPATCH[name]() for name in activated}\n",
    "    total_tool_calls_A += len(activated)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Phase 4 — manager halt rules\n",
    "    halt, halt_reason = False, \"\"\n",
    "    if confidence >= CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD:\n",
    "        halt, halt_reason = True, \"confidence\"\n",
    "    elif not activated:\n",
    "        halt, halt_reason = True, \"exhausted\"\n",
    "    elif round_t >= T_MAX:\n",
    "        halt, halt_reason = True, \"cap\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    latency_ms = (time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "    r = RoundResultA(\n",
    "        round=round_t,\n",
    "        query=query,\n",
    "        activated_tools=activated,\n",
    "        tool_scores=scores,\n",
    "        tool_results=tool_results,\n",
    "        confidence=confidence,\n",
    "        halt=halt,\n",
    "        halt_reason=halt_reason,\n",
    "        llm_calls=total_llm_calls_A,\n",
    "        latency_ms=latency_ms,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    results_A.append(r)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"Round {round_t}: confidence={confidence}  activated={activated}\")\n",
    "    score_str = \"  \".join(f\"{n}={s:.2f}\" for n, s in scores.items())\n",
    "    print(f\"  scores: {score_str}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  tool_results: {list(tool_results.keys())}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  halt={halt} reason={halt_reason!r}  latency={latency_ms:.1f}ms\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if halt:\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total LLM calls (investigator): {total_llm_calls_A}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total tool calls:               {total_tool_calls_A}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Approach B — LangChain ReAct\n",
    "\n",
    "Tool selection: LLM reads tool docstrings as part of its context, reasons about which tool to call, outputs a structured `tool_call`.\n",
    "\n",
    "No embeddings. No cosine matching. The LLM decides everything including which tool to use next.\n",
    "LangChain manages the Reason → Act → Observe → Reason loop."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 3B: Define tools with @tool decorator ────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# LangChain reads the function name + docstring + type hints to build\n",
    "# the JSON schema it sends to the LLM.\n",
    "# The function body is the actual tool execution — plain Python, no ML.\n",
    "\n",
    "from langchain_core.tools import tool\n",
    "\n",
    "@tool\n",
    "def flow_log_tool(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Returns the step-by-step routing flow trace for a document.\n",
    "    Shows which routing steps executed, which step failed, and at what timestamp.\n",
    "    Use this FIRST when investigating any routing failure — it tells you where the\n",
    "    process stopped.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return _call_flow_log(payload_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@tool\n",
    "def kafka_offset_tool(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Reports whether a document message was produced to Kafka and whether it was\n",
    "    ever consumed downstream. Use this when the flow log shows RoutingPublishStep\n",
    "    failed or when you suspect a delivery failure.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return _call_kafka_offset(payload_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@tool\n",
    "def routing_decision_tool(payload_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Returns the routing decision record: routing method used, destination PostURL,\n",
    "    buyer orgId, and whether a valid routing rule was matched.\n",
    "    Use this when the flow log shows the routing step failed to find a destination.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return _call_routing_decision(payload_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@tool\n",
    "def org_config_tool(org_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Returns the buyer organisation's current OrgPreferences: active PostURL,\n",
    "    routing flags, and last-modified timestamp.\n",
    "    Use this when routing_decision_tool shows destination_url is null or empty\n",
    "    to check if the PostURL was ever configured.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return _call_org_config(org_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "TOOLS_B = [flow_log_tool, kafka_offset_tool, routing_decision_tool, org_config_tool]\n",
    "print(f\"Registered {len(TOOLS_B)} tools for LangChain ReAct:\")\n",
    "for t in TOOLS_B:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {t.name}: {t.description[:80]}...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 4B: LangChain ReAct agent setup ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (or SAP AI Core credentials in production)\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from langchain_anthropic import ChatAnthropic\n",
    "from langchain.agents import create_react_agent, AgentExecutor\n",
    "from langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\n",
    "from langchain_core.callbacks import BaseCallbackHandler\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Callback to track LLM calls and tool calls for fair comparison ────────────\n",
    "class UsageTracker(BaseCallbackHandler):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.llm_calls = 0\n",
    "        self.tool_calls = []\n",
    "        self.tool_scores = {}   # not available in ReAct — LLM decides, no scores\n",
    "\n",
    "    def on_llm_start(self, *args, **kwargs):\n",
    "        self.llm_calls += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    def on_tool_start(self, serialized, input_str, **kwargs):\n",
    "        tool_name = serialized.get(\"name\", \"unknown\")\n",
    "        self.tool_calls.append(tool_name)\n",
    "        print(f\"  [ReAct] tool_call: {tool_name}({input_str[:60]})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── LLM (production: claude-4.6-sonnet via SAP AI Core) ──────────────────────\n",
    "# Swap ChatAnthropic for ChatOpenAI + base_url if using SAP AI Core\n",
    "llm_B = ChatAnthropic(\n",
    "    model=\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n",
    "    api_key=os.getenv(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"\"),\n",
    "    temperature=0.0,\n",
    "    max_tokens=1500,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── ReAct prompt ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "react_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n",
    "    (\"system\",\n",
    "     \"You are an investigation agent diagnosing B2B document routing failures. \"\n",
    "     \"Use the available tools to gather evidence step by step. \"\n",
    "     \"Start with the flow log, then follow the evidence. \"\n",
    "     \"When you have identified the root cause with high confidence, conclude with: \"\n",
    "     \"'Root cause: <cause>. Fix: <fix>.' \"\n",
    "     \"Document: {payload_id}. Buyer org: {org_id}.\"),\n",
    "    (\"human\",  \"{input}\"),\n",
    "    (\"placeholder\", \"{agent_scratchpad}\"),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Agent + executor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "llm_with_tools_B = llm_B.bind_tools(TOOLS_B)\n",
    "agent_B = create_react_agent(llm_with_tools_B, TOOLS_B, react_prompt)\n",
    "\n",
    "tracker_B = UsageTracker()\n",
    "executor_B = AgentExecutor(\n",
    "    agent=agent_B,\n",
    "    tools=TOOLS_B,\n",
    "    verbose=True,\n",
    "    max_iterations=T_MAX,\n",
    "    callbacks=[tracker_B],\n",
    "    return_intermediate_steps=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"LangChain ReAct agent ready.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Cell 5B: Run Approach B ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Approach B: LangChain ReAct ===\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "result_B = executor_B.invoke({\n",
    "    \"input\":      QUESTION,\n",
    "    \"payload_id\": PAYLOAD_ID,\n",
    "    \"org_id\":     ORG_ID,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "latency_B_ms = (time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"Final output: {result_B['output']}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"Total LLM calls:   {tracker_B.llm_calls}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total tool calls:  {len(tracker_B.tool_calls)}  →  {tracker_B.tool_calls}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total latency:     {latency_B_ms:.1f}ms\")"
   ]
  },
